00:00:47.534 --> 00:00:50.957
<i>Let me tell you a story about a young man called Oliver.</i>


00:00:50.989 --> 00:00:55.374
<i>There's no singing. No dancing.
And definitely no happy ending.</i>


00:00:56.205 --> 00:00:58.062
<i>But before we get to me,</i>


00:00:58.095 --> 00:01:00.399
<i>this all started with a thief
called Tom Chitling.</i>


00:01:09.134 --> 00:01:10.254
There he is!


00:01:10.287 --> 00:01:11.823
Stop! Stop!


00:01:30.031 --> 00:01:31.696
Let's go!


00:02:01.581 --> 00:02:03.919
- Come here! Where is it?
- I don't have it.


00:02:47.791 --> 00:02:50.383
<i>Growing up,
it was just me and Mum.</i>


00:02:50.414 --> 00:02:53.838
<i>We didn't have a lot,
but we had our imagination.</i>


00:02:54.638 --> 00:02:56.655
Where'd you take us
today, Oliver?


00:02:56.686 --> 00:02:59.566
The beach.
And we had an ice cream.


00:02:59.597 --> 00:03:01.359
Mmm, delicious.


00:03:02.318 --> 00:03:05.261
I took us
to the circus.


00:03:05.294 --> 00:03:07.951
Wow. Elephants.


00:03:07.982 --> 00:03:09.775
- Thanks, Mum.
- You're welcome.


00:03:09.805 --> 00:03:12.143
I'm gonna take us somewhere
even better tomorrow.


00:03:14.926 --> 00:03:16.527
I can't wait.


00:03:20.174 --> 00:03:21.807
What do you see?


00:03:21.837 --> 00:03:23.470
A lady swimming.


00:03:24.270 --> 00:03:25.358
What else?


00:03:26.255 --> 00:03:28.335
What does Oliver see?


00:03:28.367 --> 00:03:30.222
I don't understand,
Mum.


00:03:30.253 --> 00:03:34.798
Well, I see escape.


00:03:36.047 --> 00:03:38.703
I see a powerful woman


00:03:38.735 --> 00:03:40.783
leaving behind a life
that wasn't meant for her.


00:03:42.319 --> 00:03:45.551
And all of the flowers,
they're telling us why.


00:03:47.598 --> 00:03:51.214
Anyone ever told you
you're a bit weird, Mum?


00:03:51.886 --> 00:03:55.951
Has anyone ever told you
you're a bit cheeky?


00:03:55.981 --> 00:03:57.647
Shh!


00:03:57.679 --> 00:04:01.775
Oh. We're going
to space now, are we?


00:04:01.805 --> 00:04:02.862
Yeah.


00:04:04.078 --> 00:04:07.279
I thought we were supposed to be
doing our dreams for the future.


00:04:08.847 --> 00:04:10.511
I don't get it.


00:04:10.541 --> 00:04:13.358
Well that's you.
And that's me.


00:04:13.391 --> 00:04:15.311
And we're
in a gallery.


00:04:15.341 --> 00:04:19.022
And we're looking at this painting
of you and me in a gallery


00:04:19.055 --> 00:04:21.102
looking at this painting
of you and me in a gallery.


00:04:21.134 --> 00:04:23.119
And it goes on
and on and on...


00:04:23.919 --> 00:04:25.934
<i>But nothing
lasts forever.</i>


00:04:32.461 --> 00:04:34.189
<i>Then it was just me.</i>


00:04:34.222 --> 00:04:35.918
Poor lad.


00:04:37.966 --> 00:04:39.438
Time to go, Oliver.


00:04:39.469 --> 00:04:41.134
<i>I didn't know
anyone else.</i>


00:04:42.957 --> 00:04:44.814
<i>I certainly didn't belong
with them.</i>


00:04:49.550 --> 00:04:51.023
<i>I was better off on my own.</i>


00:05:01.006 --> 00:05:02.959
Oi! Wake up.


00:05:04.302 --> 00:05:06.126
Wake up,
you little rat.


00:05:06.158 --> 00:05:08.302
Right. I've told you before,
and I'm not... Hey!


00:05:08.334 --> 00:05:09.743
I'm not gonna
tell you again!


00:05:10.317 --> 00:05:11.823
Don't you dare.


00:05:11.855 --> 00:05:13.614
Sod off,
you little scrounger!


00:05:13.646 --> 00:05:16.047
Stop sleeping
in the gallery!


00:05:16.078 --> 00:05:18.702
<i>People don't really call
me Oliver any more. They call me...</i>


00:07:13.102 --> 00:07:16.270
Congratulations, love.


00:07:16.302 --> 00:07:17.710
You've won
a little yellow square.


00:07:17.741 --> 00:07:19.405
You could see
I had my hands full.


00:07:19.438 --> 00:07:20.814
They're not my rules.
I just enforce 'em.


00:07:20.846 --> 00:07:22.222
I was right here.


00:07:22.254 --> 00:07:23.566
You was right here
for too long.


00:07:23.598 --> 00:07:25.263
I thought
you were gonna move in.


00:07:25.294 --> 00:07:27.118
Do you think
I like doing this?


00:07:27.149 --> 00:07:29.486
Actually, I do.
It makes me feel big in every way.


00:07:29.518 --> 00:07:31.311
Could you not give
the ticket to anyone else?


00:07:31.342 --> 00:07:33.070
I'm not just giving 'em
to nice people.


00:07:33.101 --> 00:07:34.702
You look like a nice person,
so I've given one to you.


00:07:34.733 --> 00:07:36.558
Please, I was literally
about to leave.


00:07:36.589 --> 00:07:37.934
You should have left earlier,
shouldn't you?


00:07:37.965 --> 00:07:39.630
I can't afford this ticket.


00:07:39.662 --> 00:07:41.679
Well, I can't afford a 4K TV,
but I wish I could.


00:07:41.709 --> 00:07:43.278
I'd like one of those.


00:07:43.309 --> 00:07:45.166
Actually, I don't even know
what it is,


00:07:45.198 --> 00:07:47.278
but I like the sound of owning it.
I wish I could have it.


00:07:47.309 --> 00:07:49.133
- Please, sir...
- Please, please, please.


00:07:49.165 --> 00:07:50.894
Don't tell me
your problems.


00:07:50.925 --> 00:07:52.813
You're gonna get another one
in a minute. Oi!


00:07:52.845 --> 00:07:55.598
Hey, stay away from that van.
That's my van, you little pig.


00:08:06.254 --> 00:08:08.079
- Here you go, miss.
- Thank you.


00:08:16.109 --> 00:08:17.486
Stop that lad!


00:08:35.309 --> 00:08:37.454
Yo, man. The bikes!


00:08:50.797 --> 00:08:52.397
Yo, likkle man!


00:08:53.870 --> 00:08:55.182
Yo!


00:08:55.885 --> 00:08:57.775
- Hey, slow up, bro.
- What?


00:08:58.671 --> 00:09:02.094
Relax, man.
The cops packed it in way back.


00:09:02.125 --> 00:09:03.471
Why are you chasing me then?


00:09:03.502 --> 00:09:05.230
'Cause you forgot
your shopping.


00:09:08.013 --> 00:09:09.230
Okay.


00:09:14.573 --> 00:09:15.662
- It's you, isn't it?
- What?


00:09:15.693 --> 00:09:17.294
Doing all this.


00:09:17.902 --> 00:09:19.790
Come on, man,
we know that it's you.


00:09:19.821 --> 00:09:23.022
We done the forensics
on your spray cans.


00:09:23.053 --> 00:09:25.293
He's a joker, this one.
But, look, listen.


00:09:25.325 --> 00:09:27.245
I am Dodge,
this is Batesy,


00:09:27.277 --> 00:09:29.133
and together we...


00:09:36.078 --> 00:09:38.094
- What about your bikes?
- Not ours, pal!


00:09:45.677 --> 00:09:47.182
Come on!


00:09:50.317 --> 00:09:52.239
Hey! Stop!


00:09:57.293 --> 00:09:58.830
I said get down!


00:10:09.805 --> 00:10:12.302
Come on.


00:10:12.333 --> 00:10:14.541
- Cracking set of pins, love.
- Look at that.


00:10:14.573 --> 00:10:16.078
What happened to him?


00:10:17.070 --> 00:10:18.415
- What was that?
- Brilliant.


00:10:18.445 --> 00:10:20.078
You two again.


00:10:20.110 --> 00:10:22.702
Oh, come on.
We're your guardian angels.


00:10:22.734 --> 00:10:24.462
Where's the other guy?


00:10:24.494 --> 00:10:26.703
Come with us. We'll sort you out
with some new gear.


00:10:26.734 --> 00:10:29.454
Or you could just stay here.
I mean, it's up to you.


00:10:30.637 --> 00:10:32.206
We got trainers as well.


00:10:33.582 --> 00:10:35.118
Really?


00:10:35.150 --> 00:10:37.197
Come on, handsome.
Follow us.


00:10:41.742 --> 00:10:44.335
- I ain't got anything worth stealing.
- Come on, mate.


00:10:44.366 --> 00:10:46.990
You can't go through
life trusting no one.


00:10:47.022 --> 00:10:48.846
Yeah, we saved
your arse once already.


00:10:48.877 --> 00:10:50.542
That was
the other guy.


00:10:50.573 --> 00:10:52.493
What, you mean Red?


00:10:52.525 --> 00:10:54.383
Yeah.
The guy in the green jacket.


00:10:55.885 --> 00:10:58.030
That's a real hero,
that one.


00:11:07.214 --> 00:11:08.686
<i>Entre, s'il vous plaît.</i>


00:11:15.790 --> 00:11:17.357
<i>Who's that?</i>


00:11:17.390 --> 00:11:19.662
Just me and Batesy.


00:11:19.694 --> 00:11:21.263
What size waist are you?


00:11:21.294 --> 00:11:23.439
<i>I'd say he's about
a 30 regular.</i>


00:11:23.470 --> 00:11:25.166
Who's that?


00:11:25.196 --> 00:11:29.230
Oh, that is the ghost
of Dodge's grandpa.


00:11:29.262 --> 00:11:32.591
Batesy, shut up.
I'll introduce you later.


00:11:37.517 --> 00:11:39.341
Let's get you
some clobber first.


00:11:39.374 --> 00:11:41.006
Uh, you do realize
I've got no money?


00:11:41.038 --> 00:11:42.926
It's all right. You can owe us.


00:11:42.957 --> 00:11:44.718
I don't like
owing people.


00:11:47.309 --> 00:11:50.990
Go on, have 'em.
Introductory special offer.


00:11:51.405 --> 00:11:54.029
- We can spare 'em.
- Where did you get all this?


00:11:54.061 --> 00:11:56.942
- Sports Warehouse.
- Oh, I lost my favorite hat on that job.


00:11:56.973 --> 00:12:00.589
Are you ever gonna stop banging
on about that hat?


00:12:00.621 --> 00:12:02.542
- Huh?
- Probably not.


00:12:02.574 --> 00:12:06.605
Have 'em. They cost us nothing,
shop's claimed insurance.


00:12:06.638 --> 00:12:09.135
Plus, them pasty legs...


00:12:10.189 --> 00:12:12.141
they're gonna give me
nightmares.


00:12:13.070 --> 00:12:16.974
Oh, better give 'em a little bit
of a shake actually.


00:12:17.006 --> 00:12:19.279
Better give 'em
a shake first, eh.


00:12:24.173 --> 00:12:26.446
Hey, Fagin.


00:12:28.589 --> 00:12:31.470
Dodge, I've told you before.


00:12:31.502 --> 00:12:34.350
You cannot bring in green kids
off the street.


00:12:34.381 --> 00:12:36.525
- I know, but Fa...
- No buts.


00:12:36.557 --> 00:12:38.029
Out he goes.


00:12:38.061 --> 00:12:40.974
Fagin, please.
This is Twist.


00:12:41.454 --> 00:12:43.246
Extreme graffiti artist.


00:12:43.278 --> 00:12:44.910
Reaching places
others can't reach.


00:12:44.941 --> 00:12:46.862
Tags under moving cranes
and that.


00:12:46.894 --> 00:12:49.678
Like what's his face, uh...
Banksy. Yeah.


00:12:49.710 --> 00:12:52.431
Reaching places other people
can't reach, eh?


00:12:53.261 --> 00:12:56.622
The problem with graffiti is,
is you can't move it.


00:12:56.653 --> 00:12:59.343
What's the point in a painting
if it's always in the same place?


00:12:59.374 --> 00:13:02.254
The higher up I put my work,
the more people can see it.


00:13:02.990 --> 00:13:06.222
That's the point.
It doesn't belong to anybody.


00:13:06.253 --> 00:13:08.591
An idealist, eh?


00:13:08.621 --> 00:13:10.701
All property is theft.


00:13:11.341 --> 00:13:14.670
In my case,
that's literally true.


00:13:15.725 --> 00:13:18.317
Tell me, Mr. Idealist,


00:13:18.861 --> 00:13:21.166
how's virtue treating you?


00:13:21.198 --> 00:13:23.277
Is it filling your stomach?


00:13:23.310 --> 00:13:25.518
Can it give you
a hug on a cold night?


00:13:25.549 --> 00:13:28.878
Ideals are useless.
They're like appendix.


00:13:29.965 --> 00:13:31.213
Cut 'em out.


00:13:31.245 --> 00:13:32.365
He's fast.


00:13:32.398 --> 00:13:34.734
He left the Old Bill for dust.


00:13:34.765 --> 00:13:37.101
I thought maybe
we could train him up


00:13:37.134 --> 00:13:39.438
seeing as
we have a vacancy.


00:13:39.470 --> 00:13:40.877
I'm not a thief.


00:13:40.909 --> 00:13:43.822
What, you've never stole
a sarnie from Tescos?


00:13:43.853 --> 00:13:47.117
I don't need to. They chuck out
enough if you know where to look.


00:13:47.149 --> 00:13:49.229
Oh, living the dream.


00:13:49.261 --> 00:13:51.565
We all have to start somewhere,
don't we?


00:13:51.597 --> 00:13:54.446
It wasn't so long ago that you
were stealing credit card details.


00:13:54.478 --> 00:13:55.917
Uh, it's called phishing.


00:13:55.950 --> 00:13:58.093
It's called surviving.


00:13:58.126 --> 00:14:01.006
It's what we do
to survive.


00:14:01.933 --> 00:14:04.398
- Suppose.
- Bravo.


00:14:04.429 --> 00:14:05.774
You need a place to stay?


00:14:08.462 --> 00:14:09.614
No. Thank you.


00:14:10.446 --> 00:14:13.134
Cheers for the clothes.
I'll pay you back.


00:14:17.837 --> 00:14:20.077
That's
a really decent copy.


00:14:20.110 --> 00:14:22.926
I've seen the original tons
of times at the Tate.


00:14:22.956 --> 00:14:24.078
No, you haven't.


00:14:30.798 --> 00:14:33.262
I tell you what.
I'll cook tonight, Dodge.


00:14:33.293 --> 00:14:35.405
What do you want,
spaghetti or beef burgers?


00:14:35.436 --> 00:14:37.037
- I love the...
- Ah, nah.


00:14:37.069 --> 00:14:38.509
Come on. Do me a flavor, Fag.


00:14:38.541 --> 00:14:41.293
You know I'm 72% vegan.
Meat is a treat.


00:14:41.325 --> 00:14:44.685
Doesn't matter what you eat
so long as you eat together.


00:14:44.718 --> 00:14:47.886
Because, as I've always said,
the most important thing


00:14:47.917 --> 00:14:50.445
is the family
that eats together...


00:14:50.477 --> 00:14:52.397
...stays together.


00:14:52.429 --> 00:14:54.190
Yeah. Right.


00:15:03.021 --> 00:15:05.037
Oi! Mate.


00:15:05.996 --> 00:15:07.630
I just wanted to...


00:15:09.006 --> 00:15:10.510
Stand there gawping
like a fish?


00:15:11.245 --> 00:15:13.453
If you could speak sometime
soon that'd be great


00:15:13.484 --> 00:15:14.957
- 'cause I've got somewhere to go.
- I'm sorry.


00:15:14.988 --> 00:15:16.813
I didn't realize you,
you were a...


00:15:16.846 --> 00:15:18.413
And I didn't recognize you
with clothes on.


00:15:18.446 --> 00:15:19.885
I just wanted to say thanks.


00:15:19.917 --> 00:15:21.486
You're welcome.


00:15:22.605 --> 00:15:24.045
Is that everything?


00:15:25.646 --> 00:15:27.214
I'll take that as a yes.


00:16:54.476 --> 00:16:56.397
The boy's an artist.


00:16:56.429 --> 00:16:58.318
So, what do you see?


00:16:58.349 --> 00:17:01.005
A loner with a cracking pair
of trainers?


00:17:01.934 --> 00:17:04.366
Well, that's disappointing.
You missed the point.


00:17:07.021 --> 00:17:08.942
Can you get up there?


00:17:08.973 --> 00:17:10.957
Please. If he can...


00:17:11.598 --> 00:17:14.062
- Yeah.
- Some boys like respect.


00:17:14.893 --> 00:17:18.317
Some boys like being
in the pecking order.


00:17:18.349 --> 00:17:19.566
But this one...


00:17:20.174 --> 00:17:22.636
he wants something
that he's missing.


00:17:22.668 --> 00:17:24.110
A smartphone?


00:17:26.476 --> 00:17:27.917
He wants love.


00:17:27.949 --> 00:17:30.094
So let's give it
to him.


00:18:04.653 --> 00:18:06.734
Glad I climbed up
this side.


00:18:06.765 --> 00:18:07.853
Sorry!


00:18:07.886 --> 00:18:09.999
There's no toilet
up here.


00:18:10.478 --> 00:18:12.238
Love what you've done
with the place.


00:18:12.269 --> 00:18:14.478
It's just while
I'm doing this one here.


00:18:17.100 --> 00:18:18.733
Gonna offer me
a cup of tea then, or...


00:18:18.765 --> 00:18:21.166
I could do you cream crackers
and chocolate spread.


00:18:21.196 --> 00:18:22.830
Ooh, nutritious.


00:18:24.716 --> 00:18:26.637
I thought you were
a guy, by the way.


00:18:26.670 --> 00:18:28.494
That's why I was being
weird earlier.


00:18:28.524 --> 00:18:29.741
You say
the sweetest things.


00:18:29.772 --> 00:18:32.205
No, no. I wasn't...


00:18:32.238 --> 00:18:34.670
I mean, I just...


00:18:34.702 --> 00:18:38.125
- The way you move...
- Like a guy? Yeah. I get it.


00:18:38.862 --> 00:18:41.902
- I don't mean to offend you.
- Oh, why would that offend me?


00:18:41.933 --> 00:18:43.053
Just guys are more strong.


00:18:43.724 --> 00:18:45.549
Not that girls aren't strong.


00:18:45.582 --> 00:18:47.054
Girls are strong as well.


00:18:47.086 --> 00:18:48.974
Just guys tend to be...
I don't know.


00:18:49.006 --> 00:18:50.989
Not much of
a smooth talker, are we?


00:18:51.597 --> 00:18:53.358
Best stick to climbing
I think.


00:18:55.182 --> 00:18:56.814
How come you're so good
at climbing anyway?


00:19:00.396 --> 00:19:03.245
When I was younger,
I felt safer up high.


00:19:04.396 --> 00:19:05.998
People couldn't find me.


00:19:08.110 --> 00:19:09.901
So I taught myself
to climb.


00:19:10.381 --> 00:19:12.526
And you've been a loner
on a roof ever since?


00:19:13.196 --> 00:19:14.957
Suits me just fine.


00:19:16.301 --> 00:19:17.805
Well, you can't stay
up here forever.


00:19:18.220 --> 00:19:20.749
Isn't there things you wanna
see, things you wanna experience?


00:19:20.782 --> 00:19:22.414
Must get pretty boring.


00:19:22.445 --> 00:19:24.046
I can go anywhere I want.


00:19:25.549 --> 00:19:26.894
- What?
- See.


00:19:39.821 --> 00:19:41.262
I can imagine.


00:19:41.293 --> 00:19:44.301
Well, I'm here
in real life,


00:19:44.716 --> 00:19:47.405
and I've come to invite you
to a real-life dinner.


00:19:47.436 --> 00:19:49.005
Me and you?


00:19:51.020 --> 00:19:53.357
Come to Fagin's,
tonight at 7:00.


00:19:54.190 --> 00:19:55.853
And you never know,


00:19:55.885 --> 00:19:58.479
we might just be better
company than your paintings.


00:20:34.414 --> 00:20:35.694
What am I doing?


00:20:35.726 --> 00:20:37.389
What does Oliver see?


00:20:39.310 --> 00:20:40.302
Mum?


00:20:44.684 --> 00:20:46.093
Can't be by yourself forever.


00:20:51.341 --> 00:20:53.484
You're late.


00:20:53.516 --> 00:20:55.757
Is that any way to greet
your favorite supplier?


00:20:59.500 --> 00:21:01.133
What happened to Tom?


00:21:01.676 --> 00:21:03.533
He screwed up.
That's what happened.


00:21:04.366 --> 00:21:07.214
My kids are not disposable.


00:21:07.246 --> 00:21:09.806
That's exactly what they are,
my old friend.


00:21:10.541 --> 00:21:13.357
No friends, no family.
No questions.


00:21:21.164 --> 00:21:23.117
For complications.


00:21:29.452 --> 00:21:31.692
Did you get my envelope?


00:21:31.725 --> 00:21:33.230
What, this?


00:21:35.021 --> 00:21:36.654
When has it ever been
that easy, eh?


00:21:38.028 --> 00:21:39.468
I want in.


00:21:39.501 --> 00:21:41.389
I know you're pulling
a job.


00:21:41.421 --> 00:21:43.213
You're hitting Losberne.


00:21:43.692 --> 00:21:45.324
I want a cut.


00:21:45.357 --> 00:21:46.540
I was gonna tell you.


00:21:46.573 --> 00:21:47.726
Of course you were.


00:21:47.756 --> 00:21:49.485
Let me make it
easy for you.


00:21:49.517 --> 00:21:50.862
Whatever's in there...


00:21:51.949 --> 00:21:53.805
seems very important
to your little plan.


00:21:53.837 --> 00:21:56.077
Question is, are we gonna do it
the easy or the hard way?


00:22:05.805 --> 00:22:07.373
Partners.


00:22:14.285 --> 00:22:16.813
Partners. Now...


00:22:19.210 --> 00:22:19.629
the envelope.


00:22:20.652 --> 00:22:21.837
I think I'll keep it.


00:22:22.925 --> 00:22:25.358
Just in case
of future complications.


00:22:43.150 --> 00:22:44.974
Yeah.


00:22:45.004 --> 00:22:48.621
Took your bloody...
Oh, my giddy aunt.


00:22:48.653 --> 00:22:50.989
What is happening
with your barnet?


00:22:51.021 --> 00:22:53.485
Sorry.
Sorry, sorry, sorry.


00:22:53.516 --> 00:22:56.206
Come on, look, look.
Welcome, Twist.


00:22:56.237 --> 00:23:00.558
Let me take your jean shirt,
jacket for you. There we go.


00:23:02.220 --> 00:23:03.917
- Come on.
- Ah.


00:23:03.948 --> 00:23:05.772
Glad you could make it,
mate.


00:23:05.805 --> 00:23:08.269
Oh, Twist.
Come and sit next to me.


00:23:11.854 --> 00:23:14.957
Oh, blimey, look. Nancy,
take his beautiful flowers


00:23:14.989 --> 00:23:16.270
and put them in some water.


00:23:17.613 --> 00:23:18.733
Mmm.


00:23:21.389 --> 00:23:23.052
He can call me that.


00:23:23.085 --> 00:23:24.365
- You don't.
- Understood.


00:23:24.397 --> 00:23:27.821
I am starving.


00:23:27.853 --> 00:23:29.261
Dodge, please.


00:23:29.293 --> 00:23:31.022
Fagin, can we just
talk about something?


00:23:31.054 --> 00:23:33.230
Can we talk about our boy,
Batesy here,


00:23:33.260 --> 00:23:35.085
stealing my food
from under my bed?


00:23:35.116 --> 00:23:37.036
- Grass.
- Thief.


00:23:37.068 --> 00:23:39.694
- Okay, we're all thieves.
- Yeah, be a better one is the point.


00:23:39.724 --> 00:23:41.836
All right. Okay, okay.


00:23:41.869 --> 00:23:44.110
Uh, Twist,


00:23:44.141 --> 00:23:47.564
I want you to say a few words
because it's a tradition.


00:23:47.597 --> 00:23:50.126
About how thankful you are.


00:23:51.436 --> 00:23:55.117
Well, thanks for having me
round for dinner, I suppose.


00:23:55.149 --> 00:23:57.869
I can't remember the last time
that I sat down...


00:23:57.900 --> 00:23:59.566
Like a family?


00:24:00.589 --> 00:24:02.606
We're all orphans here.


00:24:08.301 --> 00:24:09.710
All right,
that's the thanks.


00:24:09.740 --> 00:24:11.373
Cool, um,
can we bloody eat now?


00:24:11.405 --> 00:24:13.454
- Yes! Eat. Eat.
- All right!


00:24:13.484 --> 00:24:15.404
- Eat.
- All right, all right.


00:24:15.437 --> 00:24:17.198
Let's go.


00:24:17.228 --> 00:24:18.702
Mmm.


00:24:26.925 --> 00:24:29.326
It appears that
you're a connoisseur of beauty.


00:24:29.997 --> 00:24:34.638
Yeah. I saw you in my office
admiring my collection, Mr. Twist.


00:24:35.725 --> 00:24:37.645
Can I stop using that name?


00:24:37.677 --> 00:24:40.013
It makes me sound
as though I'm in a casino.


00:24:41.004 --> 00:24:42.284
What else can I call you?


00:24:43.085 --> 00:24:44.108
Oliver.


00:24:44.140 --> 00:24:46.764
Oliver. Well, Oliver,


00:24:46.796 --> 00:24:49.100
your artwork is impressive.


00:24:49.133 --> 00:24:50.798
They're just copies.


00:24:50.829 --> 00:24:53.485
No, nothing is just a copy.
We always put a little bit


00:24:53.516 --> 00:24:55.533
of soul into everything,
don't you think?


00:24:56.749 --> 00:24:59.213
- Yeah, I suppose.
- When I was your age,


00:24:59.244 --> 00:25:01.293
I wanted to be an artist,
just like you.


00:25:01.773 --> 00:25:04.045
But my father was tasteless.
A bully.


00:25:04.076 --> 00:25:05.806
Oh, I'm sorry.


00:25:05.836 --> 00:25:08.685
Why sorry?
This is all my art, and Nancy...


00:25:09.868 --> 00:25:11.501
is my masterpiece.


00:25:11.917 --> 00:25:13.997
She needs someone to train with.


00:25:14.029 --> 00:25:16.301
Someone who can keep up
with her.


00:25:17.068 --> 00:25:21.228
- So you all just do whatever you want?
- Yes. But together.


00:25:21.261 --> 00:25:22.700
We never work alone.


00:25:22.732 --> 00:25:26.284
You know, we live together,
we eat together.


00:25:26.316 --> 00:25:28.044
Because the family
that eats together...


00:25:28.077 --> 00:25:29.932
Stays together. I know.


00:25:32.108 --> 00:25:33.197
Watch this,
watch this.


00:25:34.189 --> 00:25:36.014
Got a little surprise
for you.


00:25:36.044 --> 00:25:37.549
- For me?
- Yeah.


00:25:47.597 --> 00:25:48.909
Come on, then.


00:25:49.517 --> 00:25:51.853
You ready?
We're going out.


00:25:52.396 --> 00:25:53.998
Come on.


00:25:54.028 --> 00:25:56.877
Make sure you bring him back
in one piece.


00:26:07.277 --> 00:26:09.069
Don't you guys
ever feel bad?


00:26:09.645 --> 00:26:12.077
What? No.


00:26:12.109 --> 00:26:14.477
Look, the people that
we target are criminals anyway.


00:26:14.508 --> 00:26:17.198
So, it's justified,
innit?


00:26:17.228 --> 00:26:20.108
Think of Fagin
as good old Robin Hood


00:26:20.141 --> 00:26:21.773
and we're his Merry Men.


00:26:21.804 --> 00:26:23.053
Hmm.


00:26:49.741 --> 00:26:51.278
Oliver.


00:26:52.397 --> 00:26:53.644
Oliver.


00:26:53.677 --> 00:26:56.078
Hey, wake up. Come on.


00:26:57.485 --> 00:26:59.406
Get changed.
We're going out.


00:27:01.453 --> 00:27:02.893
Okay, give me a sec.


00:27:08.717 --> 00:27:11.214
- So, are you sticking around?
- Yeah, I think I will.


00:27:11.245 --> 00:27:13.069
You sure
you wanna do this?


00:27:13.101 --> 00:27:15.885
Yeah. It's nice
to belong to something.


00:27:16.749 --> 00:27:18.317
Trust me, you'll be fine.


00:27:31.821 --> 00:27:33.229
Morning, Dr. Losberne.


00:27:35.500 --> 00:27:36.685
Good morning.


00:27:40.589 --> 00:27:43.693
Dr. Crispin Losberne.


00:27:45.644 --> 00:27:47.661
Curator, art dealer


00:27:47.692 --> 00:27:51.244
and connoisseur
of 18th-century painters.


00:27:51.277 --> 00:27:53.805
He's very predictable,
which helps.


00:27:53.836 --> 00:27:59.053
Gets up every morning and leaves
for work at eight o'clock sharp.


00:27:59.085 --> 00:28:01.709
<i>He looks at his messages</i>


00:28:01.741 --> 00:28:05.645
<i>and he puts his phone away in the
right-hand pocket of his coat.</i>


00:28:05.676 --> 00:28:08.588
- Flat white.
- <i>Pays the barista.</i>


00:28:08.621 --> 00:28:10.445
Then he drinks his coffee.


00:28:10.477 --> 00:28:12.237
- Hmm.
- What's all this about?


00:28:12.268 --> 00:28:14.540
Well, we're gonna borrow
his phone.


00:28:14.572 --> 00:28:17.485
And have it back in his pocket
before he knows it's gone.


00:28:17.516 --> 00:28:18.956
But why?


00:28:18.989 --> 00:28:20.781
He took everything from me.


00:28:20.813 --> 00:28:21.997
Everything.


00:28:23.692 --> 00:28:26.476
And I'm going
to return the favor.


00:28:26.987 --> 00:28:30.253
First thing, we need
to hack Losberne's phone.


00:28:30.829 --> 00:28:33.133
Oh, and as far as the day
is concerned,


00:28:33.164 --> 00:28:34.604
it's all performance art.


00:28:34.637 --> 00:28:38.030
And the performance
will be given by Nancy.


00:28:40.428 --> 00:28:41.710
Oh!


00:28:41.740 --> 00:28:43.052
I am such a klutz.


00:28:43.085 --> 00:28:45.004
Let me help.
I've got tissues in my bag.


00:28:45.037 --> 00:28:46.510
You absolutely must
let me help.


00:28:46.541 --> 00:28:48.909
God, it's all over
your lovely jacket.


00:28:48.941 --> 00:28:50.350
Oh, I'm so stupid.


00:28:55.276 --> 00:28:56.780
I was on my way
to the Royal Academy


00:28:56.813 --> 00:28:58.285
to see
the Gainsborough exhibition.


00:28:58.316 --> 00:29:00.013
- Really.
- Oh, have you been?


00:29:02.605 --> 00:29:04.525
As a matter of fact,
I curated it.


00:29:04.556 --> 00:29:07.373
- Really?
- Oh, yes. Come on.


00:29:07.404 --> 00:29:09.614
- <i>Dodge, you got it yet?</i>
- Yeah, plugging in.


00:29:10.668 --> 00:29:13.964
All right.
On its way, Batesy.


00:29:13.996 --> 00:29:16.269
I'm quite a mover and shaker
in the art world.


00:29:16.300 --> 00:29:17.325
I have my own place.


00:29:17.357 --> 00:29:18.606
You have
your own gallery?


00:29:19.565 --> 00:29:21.228
<i>That working, Bates?</i>


00:29:21.260 --> 00:29:23.342
You don't ever need interns,
do you?


00:29:23.373 --> 00:29:24.492
Never say never.


00:29:26.221 --> 00:29:27.533
<i>Come on, Batesy.
Hurry up.</i>


00:29:27.564 --> 00:29:29.197
I'll give you my card.


00:29:29.229 --> 00:29:31.277
<i>I'm going as quick as I can.</i>


00:29:31.307 --> 00:29:32.589
It's in my jacket.


00:29:32.621 --> 00:29:33.773
Oh.


00:29:35.533 --> 00:29:37.069
<i>We need
to speed this up.</i>


00:29:37.101 --> 00:29:39.501
Yes, of course.


00:29:41.356 --> 00:29:42.765
- Oh.
- Bit wet.


00:29:42.796 --> 00:29:44.492
Hurry up,
hurry up, hurry up.


00:29:44.525 --> 00:29:46.125
Pop by anytime.


00:29:47.117 --> 00:29:49.838
- Goodbye.
- Dodge, quick, he's leaving.


00:29:54.220 --> 00:29:55.342
Quickly!


00:29:55.789 --> 00:29:57.262
Yes. Let's go.


00:30:04.044 --> 00:30:05.933
Garages on Swift Road.


00:30:15.437 --> 00:30:17.166
Someone's taken my phone.


00:30:31.468 --> 00:30:32.620
Get out of my taxi!


00:30:32.652 --> 00:30:34.702
Sorry, mate.
I thought it was free.


00:30:36.716 --> 00:30:38.444
- God.
- Is that what you're looking for?


00:30:40.269 --> 00:30:42.670
Yes. Thank you.


00:30:42.700 --> 00:30:45.068
You can keep the taxi.
I'm going to walk.


00:30:45.101 --> 00:30:46.893
Cheers.


00:30:49.997 --> 00:30:51.501
Where to, guv?


00:30:53.580 --> 00:30:55.245
Not bad for your first job,
Oliver.


00:30:55.276 --> 00:30:57.452
Yeah, and that was just
the hors d'oeuvre.


00:30:58.189 --> 00:31:01.196
Batesy, keep hacking.


00:31:01.229 --> 00:31:04.141
One word from Losberne,
I wanna hear it.


00:31:04.173 --> 00:31:06.734
We need to know his every move.


00:31:07.404 --> 00:31:08.908
- Dodge?
- Yeah?


00:31:08.941 --> 00:31:10.252
Do the washing up.


00:31:10.285 --> 00:31:12.461
Oh, man.


00:31:12.492 --> 00:31:14.764
Nancy, you're going
to art school.


00:31:14.796 --> 00:31:16.269
What?


00:31:16.300 --> 00:31:18.381
It's a crash course.


00:31:18.412 --> 00:31:20.748
If you're gonna be convincing
as an art student


00:31:20.781 --> 00:31:22.605
for an evening,
or even for ten minutes,


00:31:22.636 --> 00:31:25.036
you're gonna have to know
some art to talk about.


00:31:25.932 --> 00:31:27.916
Oliver, would you mind?


00:31:27.948 --> 00:31:29.773
- Of course.
- Ah, good.


00:31:30.222 --> 00:31:32.333
But nothing beats seeing
it in the flesh.


00:31:33.836 --> 00:31:35.757
This is about
Pope Nicholas.


00:31:36.493 --> 00:31:38.029
He's fuming.


00:31:38.061 --> 00:31:39.852
And Dante's... Shit.


00:31:40.525 --> 00:31:41.581
Wha...


00:31:41.964 --> 00:31:43.501
Guard.


00:31:44.300 --> 00:31:46.156
You do realize
this gallery's free, yeah?


00:31:46.188 --> 00:31:48.428
He's worked here
for years. He hates me.


00:31:48.460 --> 00:31:50.412
He's always throwing me out
for sleeping here.


00:31:51.852 --> 00:31:54.221
Get up.
Here, I got you.


00:31:55.757 --> 00:31:57.133
He doesn't scare me.


00:32:00.045 --> 00:32:01.581
Shall we...


00:32:11.276 --> 00:32:12.622
Millais's a genius.


00:32:13.582 --> 00:32:17.101
- The use of...
- Hardly gonna win the 500-meter backstroke, though, is she?


00:32:19.019 --> 00:32:20.750
I'm joking.
I know it's Ophelia.


00:32:21.900 --> 00:32:23.501
Anything else
you'd like to add?


00:32:25.067 --> 00:32:26.860
Well, personally,


00:32:26.891 --> 00:32:28.396
I think the flowers
in the painting


00:32:28.429 --> 00:32:30.317
are as important
as Ophelia herself.


00:32:30.828 --> 00:32:33.164
The floating flowers,
they represent her sorrow.


00:32:33.197 --> 00:32:35.437
And the nettles growing
around the willow,


00:32:35.468 --> 00:32:37.069
well that's...
that's her pain.


00:32:38.220 --> 00:32:39.949
Exactly.


00:32:39.980 --> 00:32:41.709
Did you do art
at school?


00:32:41.740 --> 00:32:44.844
No. It's just
common sense, innit?


00:32:44.876 --> 00:32:47.501
Well, that
and the Internet.


00:32:47.533 --> 00:32:49.741
All right.
Let's see what else you got.


00:32:59.020 --> 00:33:02.381
So, do you feel ready to be the most
convincing art student of all time?


00:33:02.412 --> 00:33:04.813
Yeah. Totally.


00:33:04.844 --> 00:33:06.924
Although no thanks
to my teacher. He was rubbish.


00:33:06.955 --> 00:33:08.268
Oi!


00:33:09.869 --> 00:33:11.022
So, uh...


00:33:12.172 --> 00:33:14.125
couldn't help
but notice old Ophelia


00:33:14.157 --> 00:33:15.885
made quite an impression
on you in there.


00:33:16.715 --> 00:33:18.254
Yeah.


00:33:19.372 --> 00:33:20.748
What was it about her?


00:33:24.428 --> 00:33:26.381
I used to go to
that gallery with my mum.


00:33:27.467 --> 00:33:28.812
She was an artist.


00:33:28.844 --> 00:33:31.276
Right.
That makes sense.


00:33:32.717 --> 00:33:34.989
- So, you did have a family?
- Just a mum.


00:33:36.204 --> 00:33:38.062
She wasn't around
for too long.


00:33:39.629 --> 00:33:41.357
Did you?


00:33:41.389 --> 00:33:42.860
Just a dad.


00:33:42.891 --> 00:33:44.588
But he was around
for too long.


00:33:47.627 --> 00:33:49.421
So why did you get
into free running then?


00:33:50.956 --> 00:33:52.206
So I could escape.


00:33:53.004 --> 00:33:54.349
Escape from what?


00:33:56.620 --> 00:33:58.508
From boys called
Oliver Twist.


00:34:04.076 --> 00:34:05.516
Come here!


00:34:06.700 --> 00:34:11.213
<i>To pull this job off, we'll
need the plans for Losberne's gallery.</i>


00:34:12.460 --> 00:34:14.380
<i>Oh, not
the caterpillar tash.</i>


00:34:14.411 --> 00:34:15.980
- Hello.
- Good morning, sir.


00:34:16.013 --> 00:34:17.741
We spoke on the telephone


00:34:17.773 --> 00:34:20.717
about your conversion
of number 30.


00:34:20.748 --> 00:34:22.188
The Losberne Gallery?


00:34:22.221 --> 00:34:24.877
I have bought
the building opposite


00:34:24.909 --> 00:34:28.844
and I want you to make it modern
like number 30.


00:34:28.876 --> 00:34:31.756
I have the plans here. I can show
you what we did for Dr. Losberne.


00:34:31.787 --> 00:34:33.420
Follow me.


00:34:35.981 --> 00:34:38.828
Yes. Very nice,
very nice.


00:34:41.868 --> 00:34:42.861
<i>Da.</i>


00:34:42.892 --> 00:34:45.804
11:05 on the dot, Fagin.


00:34:45.835 --> 00:34:47.468
Just like you said.


00:34:58.605 --> 00:35:00.493
This is private.


00:35:00.525 --> 00:35:03.021
It's okay.
I don't understand Russian, so...


00:35:04.525 --> 00:35:06.125
You want my business?


00:35:07.052 --> 00:35:09.549
Certainly.
Take your time.


00:35:09.580 --> 00:35:10.988
Thank you.


00:35:21.101 --> 00:35:24.173
No windows, reinforced walls.


00:35:25.164 --> 00:35:26.157
That's the one.


00:35:26.731 --> 00:35:28.844
That'll be
a job getting in.


00:35:28.876 --> 00:35:30.381
We don't have to do that.


00:35:30.924 --> 00:35:33.644
If we do
what I've got planned,


00:35:34.125 --> 00:35:35.693
they bring it out.


00:35:35.724 --> 00:35:37.036
Batesy, carry on.


00:35:37.067 --> 00:35:38.445
Bring what out?


00:35:39.021 --> 00:35:42.604
This is the painting
we're gonna steal.


00:35:42.636 --> 00:35:45.773
One of six paintings
by William Hogarth.


00:35:45.805 --> 00:35:48.493
That says Dotheboy's
Auction House, Fagin.


00:35:48.524 --> 00:35:50.060
Why are we casing up Losberne?


00:35:50.093 --> 00:35:51.885
The painting
was lost in a fire,


00:35:51.917 --> 00:35:54.828
but many people believed
it was a cover-up for a theft.


00:35:54.860 --> 00:35:58.029
All this time,
it's been off the radar.


00:35:58.060 --> 00:36:00.781
So you're saying
Losberne's got it?


00:36:00.813 --> 00:36:02.892
- He's the seller.
- Wait, hang about.


00:36:02.924 --> 00:36:04.460
How did he get his hands on it?


00:36:04.492 --> 00:36:07.533
Many years ago,
Losberne went into partnership


00:36:07.564 --> 00:36:09.612
with a man called
Isaac Solomon.


00:36:09.644 --> 00:36:12.044
Both of them bought
a lot of paintings.


00:36:12.076 --> 00:36:14.444
One of them was the Hogarth.


00:36:14.475 --> 00:36:16.299
But when they had it in auction,


00:36:16.331 --> 00:36:20.044
Losberne went missing
with the paintings.


00:36:20.075 --> 00:36:22.540
- Oh.
- And Solomon had nothing,


00:36:22.572 --> 00:36:25.740
and his credibility
as an art dealer was gone.


00:36:26.220 --> 00:36:29.773
Later, Losberne said
the paintings had been stolen.


00:36:29.805 --> 00:36:31.180
So my man tells me.


00:36:32.044 --> 00:36:34.605
How long have you been there?
I didn't hear you come in.


00:36:34.636 --> 00:36:36.236
You should be more careful,
Fagin.


00:36:36.268 --> 00:36:37.996
You're getting sloppy
in your old age.


00:36:41.900 --> 00:36:43.373
Oh,
it's only you two.


00:36:43.405 --> 00:36:46.829
Oliver, there's someone
I'd like you to meet.


00:36:48.587 --> 00:36:49.580
Oliver.


00:36:52.045 --> 00:36:53.325
Here, boy.


00:36:53.805 --> 00:36:55.564
This is Bullseye.


00:36:55.596 --> 00:36:56.652
Aw...


00:36:57.131 --> 00:36:59.372
You're gonna need
your hands later.


00:37:01.195 --> 00:37:02.828
Round two.


00:37:05.292 --> 00:37:06.829
Magnetic, see?


00:37:07.244 --> 00:37:09.004
Stick it on a pipe and get out.


00:37:19.596 --> 00:37:21.356
Oh, I'm so sorry.
Is it a bad time?


00:37:22.604 --> 00:37:24.012
It's the perfect time.


00:37:34.155 --> 00:37:35.884
Thank you.


00:37:36.843 --> 00:37:37.836
Bottoms up.


00:37:37.869 --> 00:37:39.277
Oh.


00:37:40.012 --> 00:37:41.421
Cheers.


00:37:47.147 --> 00:37:49.067
So, you were saying
it'd be answering the phones,


00:37:49.099 --> 00:37:50.891
doing a little bit of filing?


00:37:50.923 --> 00:37:53.260
Nothing a girl
like you couldn't handle.


00:37:53.837 --> 00:37:56.557
I did actually want
to show you some of my art.


00:37:57.292 --> 00:37:58.733
Street art, you say?


00:37:58.764 --> 00:38:00.557
Yeah,
it's just on here.


00:38:04.397 --> 00:38:05.932
<i>Let me just find them.</i>


00:38:06.604 --> 00:38:08.173
<i>Uh, yes. Okay.</i>


00:38:08.780 --> 00:38:10.125
This one is actually
based on...


00:38:10.156 --> 00:38:12.044
William Blake.
Of course.


00:38:14.156 --> 00:38:16.268
I love what you've done
with the line there.


00:38:17.420 --> 00:38:19.692
<i>These are actually
rather intriguing.</i>


00:38:19.724 --> 00:38:20.780
<i>Don't gas me.</i>


00:38:22.220 --> 00:38:23.756
Come on, girl.


00:38:23.787 --> 00:38:24.973
Give her a second.


00:38:25.004 --> 00:38:26.924
Sorry,
that's my graffiti talk.


00:38:26.956 --> 00:38:29.229
It's the only way to get taken
seriously on the street.


00:38:30.603 --> 00:38:32.237
Oh, right.


00:38:32.267 --> 00:38:34.061
Well, don't forget
your wine.


00:38:34.092 --> 00:38:36.107
Do you know, it's just going
straight through me.


00:38:36.139 --> 00:38:38.060
I must pop to
the little girls' room.


00:38:44.268 --> 00:38:45.741
Is it downstairs, or...


00:38:46.732 --> 00:38:48.012
Straight down
the stairs.


00:38:48.044 --> 00:38:49.516
The door straight
in front of you.


00:38:51.723 --> 00:38:53.612
Okay. Thanks.


00:39:09.068 --> 00:39:11.788
Oh, no. No, no, no.
He's on the move.


00:39:20.236 --> 00:39:22.988
- <i>I could have blown my hand off.</i>
- Yeah, calm down.


00:39:23.021 --> 00:39:25.260
- Everything all right?
- Yes, I'll be up in a minute.


00:39:25.293 --> 00:39:27.117
You better have brought
a spare.


00:39:27.148 --> 00:39:28.141
Uh...


00:39:32.109 --> 00:39:33.837
We just gotta get it
to her.


00:39:33.868 --> 00:39:34.893
I'll take it.


00:39:35.276 --> 00:39:36.717
I'm the climber,
right?


00:39:36.747 --> 00:39:39.020
Whatever you do,
don't drop it.


00:40:11.468 --> 00:40:13.356
Red, it's me.
Let me in.


00:40:17.292 --> 00:40:18.669
Look out.


00:40:19.947 --> 00:40:21.741
- Oh, my God.
- Be careful.


00:40:21.772 --> 00:40:23.148
Okay...


00:40:25.900 --> 00:40:27.564
What's going on
down there?


00:40:37.676 --> 00:40:38.956
Losberne Gallery.


00:40:38.988 --> 00:40:40.173
Special delivery.


00:40:40.204 --> 00:40:41.900
At this time of night?


00:40:41.932 --> 00:40:43.948
I'm right outside, mate.
Got a large package.


00:40:43.979 --> 00:40:46.571
Says, "artworks, fragile."


00:40:46.603 --> 00:40:48.876
I could leave it
on the doorstep if you want?


00:40:48.908 --> 00:40:50.476
No, no, no.
I'm coming. I'm coming.


00:40:50.508 --> 00:40:52.365
I was just in
the middle of something.


00:40:52.396 --> 00:40:53.516
One second.


00:40:54.027 --> 00:40:56.493
I'm at the window.
Where are you?


00:40:56.523 --> 00:40:58.572
<i>Um, let me
just check on that.</i>


00:40:58.604 --> 00:41:00.365
Sorry, mate. Wrong number.


00:41:10.923 --> 00:41:14.571
I wouldn't use that lav...
uh, bathroom for a bit.


00:41:15.404 --> 00:41:17.804
I'm sorry. You're going to have
to wait here for a moment.


00:41:17.836 --> 00:41:19.341
Brittles?


00:41:19.371 --> 00:41:20.812
Can you come up here, please?


00:41:29.133 --> 00:41:30.701
What is this?


00:41:34.668 --> 00:41:36.428
Search her bag.


00:41:36.972 --> 00:41:37.997
Hey!


00:41:38.667 --> 00:41:39.883
Excuse me!


00:41:44.684 --> 00:41:46.444
If that's the way
you treat all your interns,


00:41:46.475 --> 00:41:47.724
you can take
your work experience


00:41:47.755 --> 00:41:49.165
and shove it up your arse!


00:42:10.667 --> 00:42:12.300
Okay.


00:42:35.980 --> 00:42:39.052
<i>Our Dr. Losberne is gonna
get a surprise in the morning.</i>


00:42:39.083 --> 00:42:41.227
Until then,
you can take the night off.


00:42:41.260 --> 00:42:43.628
- Go out, have some fun.
- Yes!


00:42:43.660 --> 00:42:45.675
Yeah, but wait a minute.
Not too much fun


00:42:45.708 --> 00:42:48.076
because you're back
on duty at 7:00 a.m.


00:42:48.108 --> 00:42:49.163
7:00?


00:42:49.195 --> 00:42:51.019
We've all gotta be ready


00:42:51.052 --> 00:42:52.813
to move when
the phone goes.


00:42:52.843 --> 00:42:54.828
And I'll stay tuned to Losberne.


00:42:54.859 --> 00:42:58.028
Well, you know he might be
into some heavy phone sex,


00:42:58.060 --> 00:43:00.620
which means you might be in
for a steamy night, old boy.


00:43:00.651 --> 00:43:02.508
So there's this party.


00:43:02.540 --> 00:43:04.268
- What you saying?
- Red, you coming?


00:43:04.300 --> 00:43:05.740
She got plans.


00:43:09.900 --> 00:43:11.468
You did good.


00:43:24.331 --> 00:43:26.028
Mate, let's go.
Come on.


00:43:26.636 --> 00:43:27.981
Awkward.


00:43:42.540 --> 00:43:45.676
Come on, mate. Don't be such
a Debbie Downer.


00:43:45.707 --> 00:43:48.268
You know, there are
other birds in London.


00:43:48.748 --> 00:43:50.572
Come on.
Have a drink with us.


00:43:50.603 --> 00:43:52.940
No, I'm all right, mate.
Honestly.


00:43:52.971 --> 00:43:54.923
Come on.
You know you want to.


00:43:54.955 --> 00:43:56.204
Seriously, Batesy.


00:43:56.684 --> 00:43:58.061
I'm all right here.


00:43:58.923 --> 00:44:00.459
All right. Fine.


00:44:09.164 --> 00:44:10.733
- Hey.
- I said...


00:44:11.724 --> 00:44:14.028
Oi. You mug.


00:44:15.340 --> 00:44:16.812
She belongs to Sikes.


00:44:16.843 --> 00:44:18.700
You think
I don't know that?


00:44:18.731 --> 00:44:19.885
I don't belong to anyone.


00:44:27.691 --> 00:44:28.717
We'll see.


00:44:56.651 --> 00:44:59.084
Oi, Batesy!
Batesy, look out!


00:45:10.123 --> 00:45:12.172
I love coming here.


00:45:12.203 --> 00:45:14.092
You almost forget
you're in the city.


00:45:14.604 --> 00:45:16.684
How do you know
about this place?


00:45:16.715 --> 00:45:19.596
Uh, Sikes brought me
here once.


00:45:21.291 --> 00:45:22.700
Why'd you bring me
here then?


00:45:23.691 --> 00:45:26.796
Because I wanted to.
Is that okay?


00:45:27.979 --> 00:45:29.260
Hmm?


00:45:35.788 --> 00:45:37.548
Red!


00:45:49.036 --> 00:45:50.987
Seriously, why did
you bring me here?


00:45:51.019 --> 00:45:52.876
Why wouldn't
I bring you here?


00:45:52.907 --> 00:45:55.147
I don't think your girlfriend
would be too happy if she knew.


00:45:55.179 --> 00:45:57.132
Mmm, never said
she was my girlfriend.


00:45:58.635 --> 00:45:59.916
Why didn't you tell me?


00:46:00.652 --> 00:46:01.932
Tell you what?


00:46:03.052 --> 00:46:04.460
That you're only into...


00:46:04.491 --> 00:46:07.372
Girls?
Never said that either.


00:46:10.123 --> 00:46:11.467
I'm so confused.


00:46:25.547 --> 00:46:27.308
Oi! What the hell
are you doing?


00:46:38.956 --> 00:46:41.228
Hey. Don't tell anyone
about this, yeah?


00:46:41.964 --> 00:46:44.684
Red, if this is about Sikes,
you don't need to be scared.


00:46:44.716 --> 00:46:46.860
It's not me
I'm scared for.


00:47:04.204 --> 00:47:06.284
Got you!


00:47:06.315 --> 00:47:08.876
You think you're clever, don't you?
Call the police, love.


00:47:08.907 --> 00:47:11.244
- I will 'cause you're assaulting him!
- Assaulting him?


00:47:11.275 --> 00:47:14.059
- Yeah!
- This little bellend has been vandalizing property


00:47:14.092 --> 00:47:17.452
of the council with his
shitty little paintings.


00:47:17.483 --> 00:47:19.212
You wanna go as well, eh?


00:47:19.243 --> 00:47:20.523
Come on!


00:47:20.554 --> 00:47:22.667
Here they are.
Get down there, you! Go on.


00:47:22.700 --> 00:47:25.548
She's with the bellend there.
Arrest them.


00:47:25.579 --> 00:47:27.403
- Stay with them. It'll be okay.
- Come on, Son.


00:47:27.852 --> 00:47:29.100
I'll get Fagin.
Go on.


00:47:29.132 --> 00:47:30.828
Thank you.
All right.


00:47:38.764 --> 00:47:40.460
Personally I think
it's an improvement.


00:47:42.251 --> 00:47:43.405
So let me go.


00:47:44.171 --> 00:47:47.147
Unfortunately,
Metropolis Parking Solutions...


00:47:47.178 --> 00:47:49.291
That's the company
whose property you vandalized,


00:47:49.324 --> 00:47:52.109
they don't quite share
the same views.


00:47:57.356 --> 00:47:58.988
Little Ollie Twister.


00:48:04.906 --> 00:48:07.436
Look, to be honest, Oliver,
a little bit of graffiti


00:48:07.468 --> 00:48:09.740
is not really
what concerns me.


00:48:10.155 --> 00:48:12.171
You kind of running
into Warden Bumble,


00:48:12.204 --> 00:48:13.996
well that's just kind
of fortuitous for me.


00:48:14.028 --> 00:48:15.404
It's like
a happy accident.


00:48:16.139 --> 00:48:18.380
What I really wanna talk
to you about is...


00:48:21.995 --> 00:48:23.564
this man.


00:48:24.939 --> 00:48:25.964
Fagin.


00:48:26.794 --> 00:48:28.747
An alias, obviously.


00:48:28.779 --> 00:48:31.307
A once prestigious
art dealer.


00:48:31.339 --> 00:48:33.068
Then out of the blue...


00:48:33.099 --> 00:48:34.732
...vanishes.
Disappears.


00:48:35.403 --> 00:48:38.091
And since then, it seems
like he's been putting


00:48:38.124 --> 00:48:40.813
his knowledge of art
to more practical usage.


00:48:41.324 --> 00:48:44.045
Apparently he's running
quite the operation.


00:48:46.316 --> 00:48:47.629
Yeah.


00:48:48.715 --> 00:48:50.379
And what about
this lovely lady?


00:48:50.411 --> 00:48:51.916
Known associate of Fagin.


00:48:51.946 --> 00:48:53.292
Sikes.


00:48:54.763 --> 00:48:56.492
How am I supposed
to know these two?


00:48:58.314 --> 00:48:59.947
How am I supposed to...


00:49:01.547 --> 00:49:04.012
Nancy Lee, alias Red.


00:49:04.043 --> 00:49:06.955
Known associate of
both Sikes and Fagin's.


00:49:10.251 --> 00:49:11.947
It's a pretty girl,
Oliver.


00:49:17.931 --> 00:49:19.531
I can get you out of this,
you know.


00:49:20.299 --> 00:49:23.051
- Get me out of what?
- Ah, see, now that,


00:49:23.082 --> 00:49:25.387
that's exactly what I'm
hoping you're gonna tell me.


00:49:25.420 --> 00:49:27.052
Because your little friends,
your new pals,


00:49:27.084 --> 00:49:29.773
they're not all
that they seem.


00:49:30.252 --> 00:49:32.652
And to be perfectly honest,
friends of Fagin and Sikes


00:49:32.683 --> 00:49:34.572
have a nasty habit
of ending up, well...


00:49:38.059 --> 00:49:39.628
like that.


00:49:39.658 --> 00:49:41.931
Tom Chitling.
He died last month.


00:49:41.964 --> 00:49:44.332
Take a good look, Oliver.


00:49:44.363 --> 00:49:45.612
I don't even know this Sikes.


00:49:46.667 --> 00:49:48.332
Are you sure?


00:49:49.484 --> 00:49:50.989
I'm sure.


00:49:53.003 --> 00:49:54.029
Okay.


00:49:54.635 --> 00:49:56.715
Well,
you're free to go.


00:49:57.738 --> 00:50:01.003
Just be careful who you trust because
people only see what they wanna see.


00:50:03.467 --> 00:50:04.651
Off you go, then.


00:50:13.611 --> 00:50:14.956
You're late.


00:50:16.299 --> 00:50:17.803
Where's Twist?


00:50:18.891 --> 00:50:20.140
He was with you,
right, Dodge?


00:50:25.196 --> 00:50:27.596
Just wanted to get a run-in.
I lost track of time.


00:50:28.554 --> 00:50:29.868
I don't know
where Twist is.


00:50:29.899 --> 00:50:31.819
I gave them all the night off.


00:50:31.850 --> 00:50:34.571
Those paintings are going
nowhere till the morning.


00:50:34.604 --> 00:50:36.299
It is morning.
Where is he?


00:50:49.964 --> 00:50:51.756
- Who is this?
- <i>Think of me</i>


00:50:51.787 --> 00:50:53.803
<i>as the friendly uncle
you never had.</i>


00:50:53.835 --> 00:50:56.139
<i>I just wanted to make sure
you've got my number.</i>


00:50:56.780 --> 00:50:59.340
<i>In case you remember anything
about our Ms. Sikes.</i>


00:50:59.372 --> 00:51:00.621
I won't.


00:51:01.356 --> 00:51:03.500
You got some explaining
to do, boy.


00:51:05.355 --> 00:51:08.139
- Where you been, then?
- I went to a pub with Dodge and Batesy.


00:51:08.170 --> 00:51:10.603
They got back hours ago.
What happened to you?


00:51:11.595 --> 00:51:14.763
- I got arrested.
- Been having little words, have we?


00:51:14.795 --> 00:51:16.044
No, it wasn't
like that.


00:51:16.076 --> 00:51:17.708
It was this traffic warden.


00:51:17.739 --> 00:51:19.372
I wrote on his van
and he wasn't happy about it.


00:51:19.402 --> 00:51:21.196
You wrote
on his van last night?


00:51:21.227 --> 00:51:22.763
No, last week.


00:51:22.796 --> 00:51:24.459
I bumped into him
this morning...


00:51:24.491 --> 00:51:26.092
How come
the cops let you go?


00:51:26.891 --> 00:51:28.811
Did you give them
something they wanted?


00:51:28.843 --> 00:51:30.700
No, nothing.
I gave them nothing.


00:51:30.732 --> 00:51:32.108
If he grassed,
why would he come back here?


00:51:32.139 --> 00:51:33.292
Was I talking to you?


00:51:33.324 --> 00:51:35.180
- I'm just saying, I...
- Don't!


00:51:35.211 --> 00:51:37.483
- We need him.
- <i>Hello, Artnet.</i>


00:51:37.515 --> 00:51:39.595
- <i>Hello, it's Dr. Crispin Losberne.</i>
- Shh!


00:51:39.628 --> 00:51:41.643
<i>My vault is flooded, so I need
to move a painting to Dotheboy's.</i>


00:51:41.674 --> 00:51:43.371
He's on the phone
with the couriers.


00:51:43.402 --> 00:51:44.748
They're arranging a pickup.


00:51:44.779 --> 00:51:46.219
<i>One second.</i>


00:51:47.531 --> 00:51:49.195
Round three.


00:51:50.378 --> 00:51:52.107
The painting is gonna be
on the move.


00:51:52.138 --> 00:51:53.867
This is it.


00:51:53.898 --> 00:51:56.075
You better pray this time
it goes like clockwork.


00:51:58.732 --> 00:52:01.100
Remember,
I'm watching.


00:52:09.804 --> 00:52:11.948
I'm claustrophobic,
okay.


00:52:11.979 --> 00:52:14.412
Nobody told me that
it was gonna be that small.


00:52:14.827 --> 00:52:17.388
- Quit making a fuss and get in.
- I'm not making a fuss.


00:52:17.420 --> 00:52:20.138
I'm claustrophobic.
It's an actual condition.


00:52:20.171 --> 00:52:22.667
If Batesy gets in there
and passes out,


00:52:22.699 --> 00:52:24.556
the whole plan's screwed.
What are we gonna do?


00:52:24.587 --> 00:52:26.572
Exactly. And there is
every chance


00:52:26.603 --> 00:52:28.652
that if I get in there
I will pass out.


00:52:28.683 --> 00:52:30.476
Batesy,
don't be such a baby.


00:52:30.507 --> 00:52:32.523
What are you gonna do?
Force him down?


00:52:32.555 --> 00:52:34.635
You say you're gonna do
something then don't do it.


00:52:34.666 --> 00:52:37.964
Are we gonna do this,
or you gonna stand there arguing all day?


00:52:37.995 --> 00:52:39.084
Well, he's in now.


00:52:40.234 --> 00:52:43.372
All right. Anybody tries
to moves the crate,


00:52:43.404 --> 00:52:45.900
you set off the smoke bomb
in their face.


00:52:46.731 --> 00:52:47.915
Piece of cake.


00:52:48.586 --> 00:52:50.027
All right. That's it.


00:52:52.331 --> 00:52:53.323
Let's do it then.


00:52:56.618 --> 00:52:57.708
Really?


00:53:09.355 --> 00:53:11.563
Delivery to our gallery
in W1, yeah?


00:53:11.595 --> 00:53:12.875
Yeah, copy that, darling.


00:53:12.908 --> 00:53:14.348
We just got
a few drop-offs first.


00:53:14.380 --> 00:53:15.532
Cheers, lads.


00:53:39.435 --> 00:53:41.963
I thought we were only sharing travel
with the National Gallery piece.


00:53:41.995 --> 00:53:43.531
Uh, let me see.


00:53:43.562 --> 00:53:45.196
Originally yours
was dropped off first


00:53:45.227 --> 00:53:46.572
and then on
to the National Gallery.


00:53:46.603 --> 00:53:48.268
It's just an extra
pickup, mate.


00:53:48.298 --> 00:53:49.644
It won't affect
your drop-off time.


00:53:49.674 --> 00:53:52.042
They're close together,
you see.


00:53:52.074 --> 00:53:55.915
- Chiswell Fine Arts.
- I've never heard of it.


00:54:02.507 --> 00:54:04.907
You ever heard of
a Chiswell Fine Arts, Rosie?


00:54:04.939 --> 00:54:06.475
Somewhere near here?


00:54:06.890 --> 00:54:09.099
I thought you knew all
the galleries in London.


00:54:11.979 --> 00:54:13.963
I'll google it.


00:54:19.882 --> 00:54:22.284
Can't find a Chiswell.


00:54:25.003 --> 00:54:26.763
Get me Artnet
on the phone now!


00:54:48.011 --> 00:54:49.676
What's all this?


00:54:56.298 --> 00:54:57.579
You all right?
What's occurring?


00:54:57.610 --> 00:54:59.468
- Can we get through?
- How you doing?


00:54:59.498 --> 00:55:00.908
- Yeah, fine.
- Where you from?


00:55:00.939 --> 00:55:02.475
- I'm from Fullham.
- Fullham?


00:55:02.506 --> 00:55:05.291
I've got cousins in Fullham.
You know Phil?


00:55:05.323 --> 00:55:07.243
- No.
- You must know my second cousin.


00:55:07.275 --> 00:55:09.035
- What's her name? Oh, Tracey.
- No.


00:55:09.067 --> 00:55:10.859
- Can we get through?
- Can you get through?


00:55:10.891 --> 00:55:13.003
I don't know...


00:55:13.035 --> 00:55:15.596
<i>7-4, receiving. 7-4, receiving.</i>


00:55:15.626 --> 00:55:17.452
Is there aliens?
I mean...


00:55:17.482 --> 00:55:18.891
7-4. Go ahead.


00:55:18.923 --> 00:55:21.067
<i>Just had a call from
the Losberne Gallery.</i>


00:55:21.100 --> 00:55:23.339
<i>They seem to think
they're being robbed.</i>


00:55:23.371 --> 00:55:26.315
Is it real?
Is life even real?


00:55:26.347 --> 00:55:27.787
Everything all right,
lads?


00:55:28.875 --> 00:55:30.411
Floor it!


00:55:44.618 --> 00:55:46.219
No!


00:55:47.724 --> 00:55:49.867
Sikes, no.
No, Sikes!


00:55:50.411 --> 00:55:51.916
Please, Sikes.


00:55:54.891 --> 00:55:56.011
Run!


00:55:56.972 --> 00:55:59.819
- Where is it? Give it to me.
- I didn't get it. I'm sorry.


00:55:59.851 --> 00:56:02.891
We need a distraction.
Move. Move!


00:56:07.594 --> 00:56:09.642
When I said "don't,"
that means don't go this way.


00:56:09.675 --> 00:56:12.011
- <i>...female in a red leather jacket.</i>
- Hey!


00:56:12.042 --> 00:56:14.026
Female suspect heading west
down Pass Road.


00:56:14.059 --> 00:56:16.427
<i>Officers are in pursuit.
Officers are in pursuit.</i>


00:56:29.260 --> 00:56:30.828
I'm asking you
very nicely to stop.


00:56:34.475 --> 00:56:35.724
There it is.


00:57:00.138 --> 00:57:02.060
I really need
to start going to the gym.


00:57:02.955 --> 00:57:04.075
This is...


00:57:14.699 --> 00:57:15.948
Uh...


00:57:17.642 --> 00:57:19.370
<i>Bedwin, give me an update.</i>


00:57:19.402 --> 00:57:21.611
Brownlow, we got some good news
and some bad news.


00:57:21.643 --> 00:57:24.106
- <i>Fill me in then.</i>
- Yeah, well, the bad news is I haven't got her.


00:57:24.234 --> 00:57:27.275
- <i>What's the good news?</i>
- There is no good news, really, if I'm honest.


00:57:27.307 --> 00:57:29.003
<i>Get yourself back here now.</i>


00:57:35.947 --> 00:57:37.483
Oi! Get in.


00:57:38.284 --> 00:57:40.523
- I need to work on my cardio.
- How come Twist was


00:57:40.555 --> 00:57:42.284
in the back of that van?
Should have been you.


00:57:43.179 --> 00:57:46.443
Well, I'm claustrophobic,
so we just switched places.


00:57:48.940 --> 00:57:50.284
You shouldn't have.


00:57:57.227 --> 00:57:58.764
Batesy!


00:58:34.346 --> 00:58:36.074
He should have been
back by now.


00:58:36.106 --> 00:58:38.059
Quiet. I'm trying to think.


00:58:38.508 --> 00:58:40.715
That was our one shot.


00:58:42.154 --> 00:58:44.106
It was bad luck
is all.


00:58:44.555 --> 00:58:46.059
Bad luck? There's no such thing.


00:58:46.091 --> 00:58:48.747
It was a simple plan
until that bloody Twist


00:58:48.779 --> 00:58:50.954
decided to go in the van.


00:58:57.194 --> 00:58:59.052
Mate, have you seen...


00:59:01.323 --> 00:59:02.891
What happened
to Tom Chitling?


00:59:02.923 --> 00:59:04.011
He fell.


00:59:05.770 --> 00:59:09.610
- Did you see it?
- Someone has been misinforming you, Oliver.


00:59:09.643 --> 00:59:14.059
- Don't avoid the question!
- I just don't think it's you asking the questions.


00:59:14.091 --> 00:59:16.012
Who have you been talking to?


00:59:18.667 --> 00:59:20.172
Sikes.


00:59:20.778 --> 00:59:22.987
Why don't you ask her?


00:59:24.107 --> 00:59:25.899
- Sikes!
- He's a rat!


00:59:26.379 --> 00:59:28.427
Van suddenly peels off.
They knew what was going down.


00:59:28.459 --> 00:59:29.868
- I didn't tell them anything!
- Lies!


00:59:31.915 --> 00:59:33.259
What's this, eh?


00:59:35.883 --> 00:59:37.707
Thing I need to know, Twist,


00:59:37.739 --> 00:59:39.467
is how you hold up
under a beating.


00:59:40.011 --> 00:59:41.354
I bet you fall
to pieces, eh?


00:59:41.387 --> 00:59:42.603
Fagin, make her stop.


00:59:51.146 --> 00:59:52.874
Question is,
do you want some more?


00:59:55.659 --> 00:59:56.780
Hold him.


00:59:58.123 --> 01:00:00.202
Sikes, don't make it
permanent.


01:00:00.234 --> 01:00:01.963
Right, Bullseye,
on my command.


01:00:03.402 --> 01:00:05.354
You're making a mistake.


01:00:05.834 --> 01:00:07.243
A mistake?


01:00:08.106 --> 01:00:10.028
He got in trouble
with the traffic warden.


01:00:10.059 --> 01:00:11.916
And how would
you know that, Red?


01:00:12.554 --> 01:00:13.932
'Cause I was there.


01:00:15.050 --> 01:00:16.171
What?


01:00:18.411 --> 01:00:20.267
We were on our way home
and the traffic warden


01:00:20.299 --> 01:00:22.123
came out of nowhere
and tackled him to the ground.


01:00:22.155 --> 01:00:24.107
- Just like he said.
- On your way home from where?


01:00:26.698 --> 01:00:27.787
We...


01:00:29.003 --> 01:00:30.860
We went for a swim together.


01:00:43.851 --> 01:00:45.675
If he moves, shoot him.


01:00:45.707 --> 01:00:47.755
Come with me.


01:00:47.786 --> 01:00:49.003
Bullseye, stay.


01:01:01.675 --> 01:01:03.371
This ain't like Batesy.


01:01:03.402 --> 01:01:05.386
He gets withdrawal symptoms
if he ain't plugged in.


01:01:05.419 --> 01:01:07.723
- Batesy's dead.
- What?


01:01:07.754 --> 01:01:09.035
Just like she killed Tom.


01:01:09.610 --> 01:01:11.690
- But Sikes said...
- Tom was murdered!


01:01:12.426 --> 01:01:14.570
He didn't go off
that roof by accident.


01:01:15.851 --> 01:01:17.259
How would you know that?


01:01:18.411 --> 01:01:19.660
I got a text
off that phone.


01:01:21.226 --> 01:01:22.762
Some cop gave it to me
to see if I'd turn.


01:01:22.795 --> 01:01:24.523
And did you turn?


01:01:24.555 --> 01:01:27.500
Or were you never
with this family to begin with?


01:01:28.010 --> 01:01:29.675
You call this a family?


01:01:30.379 --> 01:01:31.946
When that psycho is
out there with Red


01:01:31.979 --> 01:01:33.579
and you're pointing
a gun at me!


01:01:34.731 --> 01:01:35.947
I don't believe you.


01:01:35.978 --> 01:01:37.514
I'm gonna go find Batesy myself.


01:01:37.547 --> 01:01:39.052
You're gonna be looking
six feet under.


01:01:39.499 --> 01:01:42.283
He's right. I pushed Tom.


01:01:42.314 --> 01:01:44.170
- You lying piece...
- Please.


01:01:44.202 --> 01:01:45.995
Give me an excuse to kill you.


01:01:46.411 --> 01:01:47.627
You can't kill all of us.


01:01:48.394 --> 01:01:49.579
Let's see, shall we?


01:01:50.155 --> 01:01:52.363
Six bullets, three kids.
You do the math.


01:01:52.395 --> 01:01:54.731
We're hitting Dotheboy's.
We're getting that painting.


01:01:54.763 --> 01:01:56.619
Dotheboy's?
I think the whole plan


01:01:56.650 --> 01:01:59.146
was to get the painting
before it went there.


01:01:59.178 --> 01:02:01.387
That place
is impenetrable.


01:02:01.419 --> 01:02:03.019
You scared, old man?


01:02:03.530 --> 01:02:05.931
I'll have a plan
in four hours.


01:02:06.442 --> 01:02:09.483
Try not to kill any more
of them in the meantime.


01:02:12.138 --> 01:02:13.451
I can't promise anything.


01:02:21.898 --> 01:02:24.010
<i>Look, mate,
I believe ya.</i>


01:02:24.683 --> 01:02:27.019
<i>What Sikes did to Tom,
that's messed up.</i>


01:02:27.594 --> 01:02:29.899
But if we don't do this,
we'll lose Red too.


01:02:31.403 --> 01:02:33.163
Sikes is a loose cannon.


01:02:33.194 --> 01:02:35.243
Let's just suck it up
and get on with it, yeah?


01:02:36.938 --> 01:02:38.283
Let's do this.


01:02:44.970 --> 01:02:46.058
<i>Is he on time?</i>


01:02:46.090 --> 01:02:48.780
Like clockwork. We're on.


01:03:01.227 --> 01:03:02.891
Can I get two sugars
with that, as well?


01:03:03.626 --> 01:03:05.354
All right there, mates?
Sorry to interrupt.


01:03:05.386 --> 01:03:07.210
Can I get a Bakewell tart,
please?


01:03:07.242 --> 01:03:08.747
Sure.


01:03:09.259 --> 01:03:11.083
- It's chippy, innit?
- Yeah, I know. It's freezing.


01:03:11.115 --> 01:03:12.843
There you go. 1.50.


01:03:13.292 --> 01:03:14.634
There you go.
Keep the change.


01:03:15.882 --> 01:03:16.972
Thanks.


01:03:19.211 --> 01:03:20.522
Have a good day,
lads.


01:03:20.554 --> 01:03:21.739
See ya.


01:03:36.074 --> 01:03:39.530
<i>The painting will be under
lock and key before the auction.</i>


01:03:39.946 --> 01:03:42.891
<i>So our only chance is
during the main event.</i>


01:03:42.922 --> 01:03:45.610
<i>We'll go in at the front
and at the right moment</i>


01:03:45.643 --> 01:03:48.523
<i>execute the plan,
sending the painting your way.</i>


01:03:48.554 --> 01:03:50.571
Let's play happy families, eh?
Big smiles.


01:04:08.459 --> 01:04:10.123
Thank you.


01:04:10.154 --> 01:04:12.074
Whoa, whoa.


01:04:12.106 --> 01:04:14.123
It's the chair. Really?


01:04:14.635 --> 01:04:15.819
Jesus.


01:04:32.426 --> 01:04:34.442
There you go.


01:04:34.474 --> 01:04:37.099
<i>Dodge, once you're
inside, let Twist in.</i>


01:04:37.131 --> 01:04:39.210
<i>Then, when all hell
has broken loose,</i>


01:04:39.242 --> 01:04:40.362
<i>you know what to do.</i>


01:04:45.803 --> 01:04:47.051
Gang's all here.


01:04:55.530 --> 01:04:57.323
Don't do anything stupid.


01:05:06.283 --> 01:05:09.130
I'm glad you're finally taking
this threat seriously, Officer.


01:05:10.794 --> 01:05:12.396
Detective Inspector.


01:05:18.762 --> 01:05:20.172
How many men
have you deployed?


01:05:21.291 --> 01:05:22.635
There's 12
inside the building.


01:05:23.466 --> 01:05:25.163
Another 20 outside.


01:05:28.810 --> 01:05:30.315
Nobody is getting
this painting, Losberne.


01:05:30.346 --> 01:05:31.979
Doctor Losberne.


01:05:41.962 --> 01:05:43.594
Better you than me,
mate.


01:05:59.818 --> 01:06:01.387
<i>Lot 146.</i>


01:06:02.123 --> 01:06:03.914
William Hogarth's painting


01:06:03.946 --> 01:06:06.635
<i>A Harlot's Progress,
The Arrest.</i>


01:06:06.666 --> 01:06:09.546
Oil on canvas. 1731.


01:06:09.578 --> 01:06:11.658
Has resurfaced
after many years,


01:06:11.690 --> 01:06:14.442
as the only surviving <i>Harlot's
Progress</i> from the fire...


01:06:14.474 --> 01:06:15.979
Now.


01:06:16.555 --> 01:06:20.139
We start the reserve
price of three million pounds.


01:06:20.169 --> 01:06:21.642
Yes, madam.


01:06:23.018 --> 01:06:25.770
And you, sir? At the back there, sir? Yes.


01:06:25.803 --> 01:06:27.403
Three million two.


01:06:27.435 --> 01:06:28.971
I have three million,
200 thousand pounds.


01:06:31.241 --> 01:06:32.747
He's got a gun!


01:06:34.699 --> 01:06:36.619
- Stay calm.
- It was a trap.


01:06:36.649 --> 01:06:39.338
- They're after my painting!
- Get it back in the vault!


01:06:39.370 --> 01:06:41.035
It'll be safe.
It's the safest place.


01:06:46.315 --> 01:06:48.714
- Over there, look.
- Through that door.


01:06:53.482 --> 01:06:56.203
There's a robbery in progress.
Stay with the painting.


01:06:56.235 --> 01:06:58.091
Get it to the vault.
Let's go! Let's move.


01:07:01.322 --> 01:07:03.242
Wait, wait, wait.


01:07:03.274 --> 01:07:04.939
I'm coming with you.


01:07:04.970 --> 01:07:06.283
No one goes
down there but us.


01:07:06.314 --> 01:07:08.075
There's a robbery in progress.


01:07:08.107 --> 01:07:10.986
- Yeah, we have our procedures.
- And I have my orders.


01:07:11.019 --> 01:07:13.771
And that painting ain't going
anywhere without me.


01:07:13.803 --> 01:07:15.755
What... What's going on?


01:07:15.786 --> 01:07:18.571
- Who are you?
- Officer Dawkins, Sergeant.


01:07:18.602 --> 01:07:20.362
- Dawkins? Good.
- Yeah.


01:08:02.123 --> 01:08:04.907
Okay. You guys go that way.
You guys come with me. Let's go.


01:08:11.146 --> 01:08:12.330
You.


01:08:13.002 --> 01:08:15.371
Yes, it's me.


01:08:17.001 --> 01:08:18.954
Ah, that felt good.


01:08:34.570 --> 01:08:36.619
Good. This is good.
This is very good.


01:08:37.642 --> 01:08:39.148
Whoa, whoa, whoa.


01:08:42.410 --> 01:08:43.596
Show me the painting.


01:08:45.193 --> 01:08:46.186
Ah...


01:08:48.042 --> 01:08:49.898
I'll be honest,
not his best work.


01:08:53.738 --> 01:08:55.147
Move!


01:08:55.178 --> 01:08:56.171
Okay.


01:09:00.266 --> 01:09:02.090
Oh, you silly sausage.


01:09:02.122 --> 01:09:03.403
You're going nowhere, Son.


01:09:05.257 --> 01:09:06.763
Shit!


01:09:08.715 --> 01:09:10.730
Brownlow,
you're wrong about Twist.


01:09:10.762 --> 01:09:12.203
He's in the lift shaft.


01:09:12.234 --> 01:09:13.962
Yeah, the dirty swine.


01:09:15.466 --> 01:09:16.940
Well, move then.


01:09:20.618 --> 01:09:22.634
I'm coming for you, Twist.


01:09:22.665 --> 01:09:25.579
- No, no, no!
- If you think a lift is gonna stop me...


01:09:26.475 --> 01:09:29.291
- Oh, you got nowhere to hide, boy.
- Dodge!


01:09:29.323 --> 01:09:30.379
- You muppet.
- Dodge?


01:09:30.410 --> 01:09:32.234
You...


01:09:32.265 --> 01:09:33.322
Hurry up.


01:09:33.354 --> 01:09:34.538
- Dodge.
- Come on.


01:09:34.570 --> 01:09:35.818
Help me!


01:09:35.851 --> 01:09:37.739
- Hurry up.
- Help!


01:09:37.770 --> 01:09:39.755
- Come on.
- I'm coming!


01:09:39.787 --> 01:09:41.419
Get these bloody doors open!


01:09:50.858 --> 01:09:52.107
Hurry up, Dodge!


01:10:05.641 --> 01:10:07.146
Oi!


01:10:13.545 --> 01:10:15.081
Wait a minute.


01:10:15.113 --> 01:10:17.066
Give me a break.
You're not thinking we...


01:10:17.098 --> 01:10:19.275
- Oi! Stop!
- Come on!


01:10:21.898 --> 01:10:24.459
- Ready? Belt.
- Twist, what are you doing? This is madness.


01:10:24.489 --> 01:10:26.058
Three, two, one...


01:10:29.354 --> 01:10:30.538
Hang on!


01:10:31.338 --> 01:10:32.843
Wait, wait...


01:10:32.874 --> 01:10:34.058
Let go!


01:10:40.010 --> 01:10:41.802
Okay.


01:10:41.834 --> 01:10:43.082
Congratulations.


01:10:44.107 --> 01:10:45.227
All the best.


01:10:48.938 --> 01:10:50.827
Brownlow, you need
to get down here right now.


01:10:56.265 --> 01:10:57.514
Shit!


01:10:57.546 --> 01:11:00.906
Shit, shit!


01:11:00.938 --> 01:11:03.018
- Flippin' hell.
- Let's go up here.


01:11:04.937 --> 01:11:06.699
I think we've lost them.


01:11:06.729 --> 01:11:08.779
They wouldn't have got far,
Losberne.


01:11:08.810 --> 01:11:10.154
Well,
you better be right.


01:11:10.794 --> 01:11:12.586
- Come on. Let's go.
- Hey! Hey!


01:11:12.617 --> 01:11:14.123
Don't even think about it!
Do not move.


01:11:14.153 --> 01:11:16.425
Hello?


01:11:16.457 --> 01:11:18.506
- <i>Your delivery's here.</i>
- I didn't order anything.


01:11:19.243 --> 01:11:21.643
- Hey, don't!
- Dodge, let's go!


01:11:22.634 --> 01:11:24.106
Hey!


01:11:24.138 --> 01:11:26.155
Get after them!
Don't leave, hey!


01:11:26.185 --> 01:11:28.235
- Come back here! Come...
- Wait!


01:11:28.266 --> 01:11:31.274
Get them... Hey, stop!


01:11:31.305 --> 01:11:33.866
Stop! Make him stop!


01:11:51.307 --> 01:11:54.091
There's only one person
who could do this.


01:12:00.170 --> 01:12:01.706
<i>Batesy.</i>


01:12:01.737 --> 01:12:03.050
Enjoy your munch, did ya?


01:12:03.082 --> 01:12:05.578
You magnificent bastard.


01:12:05.611 --> 01:12:09.482
You had us worried sick, mate.
Where are ya?


01:12:09.513 --> 01:12:12.330
You know Sikes has gone
full-blown psycho, don't you?


01:12:12.362 --> 01:12:14.025
- <i>She tried to kill me.</i>
- What?


01:12:14.058 --> 01:12:15.531
We're on our way
to see her now.


01:12:15.562 --> 01:12:17.386
<i>No, don't! It ain't safe.</i>


01:12:17.418 --> 01:12:19.915
What do you mean?
We got no choice.


01:12:19.946 --> 01:12:22.091
<i>Red's with her.
We're all heading to Fagin's.</i>


01:12:23.243 --> 01:12:24.875
All right, well,
I'll meet you there.


01:12:24.907 --> 01:12:26.411
- <i>Just look after yourself.</i>
- Okay.


01:12:27.593 --> 01:12:29.642
That was Batesy. He's...


01:12:32.234 --> 01:12:33.418
Twist?


01:12:37.898 --> 01:12:39.114
Twist?


01:12:42.857 --> 01:12:44.683
You're late.
Where is he?


01:12:45.257 --> 01:12:46.986
I don't know.
We got split up.


01:12:47.017 --> 01:12:48.585
- Who's got it?
- He has.


01:12:48.618 --> 01:12:49.835
Oi!


01:12:50.762 --> 01:12:52.906
- You miss me?
- Bates.


01:12:53.482 --> 01:12:55.306
You all right?
What happened?


01:12:55.337 --> 01:12:57.451
Thought I dealt with you,
fuck's sake.


01:12:57.481 --> 01:12:59.561
- Where's Twist?
- I'm right here.


01:13:07.402 --> 01:13:09.258
You want the painting?
She's coming with me.


01:13:10.539 --> 01:13:11.979
Do you think she's worth it?


01:13:15.721 --> 01:13:16.714
Try me.


01:13:18.250 --> 01:13:19.851
Do what he says.


01:13:24.458 --> 01:13:26.539
You got more stones than
I gave you credit for.


01:13:28.329 --> 01:13:29.835
Give me that.


01:13:35.689 --> 01:13:37.642
I'll always be
a step ahead of you.


01:13:41.033 --> 01:13:42.890
You think
you can just take my girl?


01:13:44.265 --> 01:13:45.290
It's the painting, Sikes.


01:13:45.737 --> 01:13:47.946
Give me the envelope
and let him go.


01:13:49.034 --> 01:13:50.154
You sure that's it, Fagin?


01:13:55.050 --> 01:13:56.971
- What?
- The painting.


01:13:57.641 --> 01:13:59.018
Are you sure
it's the right one?


01:14:03.722 --> 01:14:05.611
Easy. Easy.


01:14:06.185 --> 01:14:07.850
I'm just reaching for my phone.


01:14:08.425 --> 01:14:10.346
You guys might wanna see this.


01:14:16.298 --> 01:14:18.155
You see,
before I got into graffiti,


01:14:18.922 --> 01:14:20.587
I used to paint.


01:14:20.618 --> 01:14:23.881
You lot mentioning Hogarth
got me inspired.


01:14:23.914 --> 01:14:25.739
It's not bad, eh, Fagin?


01:14:26.505 --> 01:14:27.690
Where is it?


01:14:28.073 --> 01:14:29.771
I walk out of here
with Red.


01:14:30.505 --> 01:14:32.298
I'll call you
and tell you where it is.


01:14:32.329 --> 01:14:33.675
She stays with me.


01:14:35.081 --> 01:14:36.682
We need the painting, Sikes.


01:14:36.713 --> 01:14:38.570
Whose side are you on?


01:14:38.602 --> 01:14:41.707
All this has got to stop.
You're done. We're done.


01:14:41.739 --> 01:14:43.723
All bets are off.


01:14:43.754 --> 01:14:46.826
Get me the envelope
and I'll let you leave.


01:15:00.298 --> 01:15:01.481
Come on.


01:15:02.378 --> 01:15:03.913
You'll let me leave?


01:15:10.154 --> 01:15:11.850
I choose how this ends.


01:15:12.873 --> 01:15:14.507
- Fagin, Fagin.
- Fagin.


01:15:15.018 --> 01:15:16.011
Fagin?


01:15:22.090 --> 01:15:23.466
Come on!


01:15:24.202 --> 01:15:26.346
Quick! Come on, Twist!


01:15:38.857 --> 01:15:40.266
Come on!


01:15:44.778 --> 01:15:46.219
You go first.


01:15:46.250 --> 01:15:47.691
I'm not going without you!


01:15:47.722 --> 01:15:49.963
Listen, jump.
I'll be right behind you.


01:15:50.473 --> 01:15:51.466
Go.


01:16:08.553 --> 01:16:10.345
Twist! Twist.


01:16:10.377 --> 01:16:11.626
Hold on, hold on.


01:16:11.657 --> 01:16:13.227
Come on!


01:16:17.994 --> 01:16:20.298
Twist! Come on.


01:16:20.330 --> 01:16:21.674
Don't let go.


01:16:29.289 --> 01:16:31.274
No! No!


01:16:34.219 --> 01:16:37.355
- Pull him up, Sikes.
- I'm sure he'll be fine. Step back!


01:16:37.385 --> 01:16:39.465
Look at him, not even strong
enough to pull himself up.


01:16:39.498 --> 01:16:42.026
- He's so weak.
- He's not weak!


01:16:42.058 --> 01:16:44.842
- You need to come with me now.
- I don't need you anymore.


01:16:44.873 --> 01:16:46.602
You think Twist is
the one for you?


01:16:46.633 --> 01:16:48.011
He's more than
you will ever be.


01:16:48.041 --> 01:16:49.739
I dragged you from the gutter,
looked after you,


01:16:49.770 --> 01:16:51.530
gave you everything
you needed.


01:16:51.561 --> 01:16:52.810
Sikes!


01:17:09.610 --> 01:17:12.843
What a fine thing
capital punishment is.


01:17:45.578 --> 01:17:47.051
Young man.


01:17:50.281 --> 01:17:52.202
I'm guessing you heard
about the reward?


01:17:56.265 --> 01:17:57.867
Be there in five.


01:18:02.889 --> 01:18:05.289
Do we know what we're meant
to be waiting for?


01:18:05.321 --> 01:18:07.499
We don't have a clue,
Bedwin.


01:18:07.529 --> 01:18:09.515
I'm sure we'll know
when we see it.


01:18:09.546 --> 01:18:11.691
He's not exactly just gonna stroll in.


01:18:11.721 --> 01:18:14.250
- He's literally just strolled in.
- All right, lads?


01:18:14.761 --> 01:18:17.161
- You hungry?
- You got a lot of nerve showing up.


01:18:17.193 --> 01:18:19.306
- Let's just nick him now.
- Calm down, Bedwin.


01:18:19.338 --> 01:18:21.002
You look like you could do
with a bacon sarnie.


01:18:21.034 --> 01:18:22.762
This might be funny to you,
but this is serious.


01:18:22.792 --> 01:18:24.009
I need your full cooperation.


01:18:24.042 --> 01:18:26.059
Whoa, whoa, whoa.
Cooperation?


01:18:26.666 --> 01:18:28.235
I've done you guys a favor.


01:18:29.001 --> 01:18:30.634
How's that?


01:18:30.666 --> 01:18:31.754
Where's the painting?


01:18:31.784 --> 01:18:33.067
I don't have it.


01:18:33.098 --> 01:18:34.602
So where is it?


01:18:34.634 --> 01:18:36.361
I'm not the criminal here.
In fact,


01:18:36.394 --> 01:18:37.898
I've done all the work
for you guys.


01:18:37.929 --> 01:18:39.786
Two bacon sarnies.


01:18:39.817 --> 01:18:41.066
- Enjoy.
- Thanks.


01:18:41.097 --> 01:18:42.730
Excuse me. I didn't order this.


01:18:42.762 --> 01:18:45.035
Oh, no, it's fine.
It's my treat.


01:18:45.065 --> 01:18:47.177
Well, that's very kind of you,
young man.


01:18:47.210 --> 01:18:50.378
- Yes, very kind.
- But don't think this is getting you out of trouble.


01:18:50.409 --> 01:18:51.722
I need you to understand
one thing.


01:18:51.753 --> 01:18:53.513
You're gonna need
to start cooperating.


01:18:56.809 --> 01:18:58.217
Oh, brilliant.


01:19:08.330 --> 01:19:10.282
Yeah, hello?
Very smart that was.


01:19:10.313 --> 01:19:11.977
<i>A wise cop
once said to me,</i>


01:19:12.008 --> 01:19:13.929
<i>"People only see
what they wanna see."</i>


01:19:13.961 --> 01:19:16.777
<i>You'll be wanting some
brown sauce with those I assume.</i>


01:19:16.808 --> 01:19:19.466
What do you mean... Hello? Hello?


01:19:22.217 --> 01:19:23.529
Brown sauce.


01:19:26.633 --> 01:19:27.913
Nah, it's...


01:19:31.433 --> 01:19:32.969
It's above
the brown sauce, Bedwin.


01:19:33.001 --> 01:19:34.507
It's above
the brown sauce.


01:19:36.553 --> 01:19:38.090
Holy shit.


01:19:52.297 --> 01:19:55.818
<i>The tale of the stolen Hogarth
in an audacious raid</i>


01:19:55.850 --> 01:19:57.802
<i>took a bizarre twist today</i>


01:19:57.832 --> 01:20:01.130
<i>when a tip-off led detectives
to a lockup in East London</i>


01:20:01.162 --> 01:20:04.970
<i>in which a large collection of
stolen artworks has been discovered.</i>


01:20:05.002 --> 01:20:09.131
<i>The lockup belongs to the art
dealer Dr. Crispin Losberne.</i>


01:20:09.705 --> 01:20:13.386
<i>Documents were also found
proving that Dr. Crispin Losberne</i>


01:20:13.417 --> 01:20:16.330
<i>is not the legal owner
of the Hogarth.</i>


01:20:16.362 --> 01:20:19.306
<i>It's alleged that
the well-established art dealer</i>


01:20:19.338 --> 01:20:22.859
<i>has been making his fortune
out of selling stolen artwork</i>


01:20:22.890 --> 01:20:25.482
<i>and faking
the ownership documentation.</i>


01:20:25.514 --> 01:20:28.906
<i>A Mr. Isaac Solomon
has been named as an accomplice.</i>


01:20:28.937 --> 01:20:32.459
<i>It's believed that this man
also goes by the name of Fagin.</i>


01:20:33.065 --> 01:20:35.658
<i>Fagin and Sikes really
had raised some good thieves.</i>


01:20:35.689 --> 01:20:38.505
<i>So good they didn't know
when they were the target.</i>


01:20:43.338 --> 01:20:45.866
<i>The envelope revealed
the true owners of the Hogarth</i>


01:20:45.897 --> 01:20:49.098
<i>and the key to the lockup where
Losberne kept the stolen paintings.</i>


01:20:59.433 --> 01:21:03.082
- Holy shit.
- <i>Even Bedwin and Brownlow deserved a break.</i>


01:21:03.112 --> 01:21:05.226
<i>In other arts-related news,</i>


01:21:05.257 --> 01:21:08.745
<i>a mystery painting arrived
with a special delivery</i>


01:21:08.776 --> 01:21:11.913
<i>for a new exhibition at
the National Gallery last week.</i>


01:21:11.945 --> 01:21:15.626
<i>The question everyone's asking
is: How did it get there?</i>


01:21:16.266 --> 01:21:19.369
<i>The painting was added
to the exhibition by mistake</i>


01:21:19.402 --> 01:21:22.538
<i>but critics have gone wild
for this unknown artist</i>


01:21:22.569 --> 01:21:25.290
<i>and have demanded
the piece remains on display.</i>


01:21:30.474 --> 01:21:31.914
There you go, Mum.


01:21:35.817 --> 01:21:39.753
<i>In fact, people can't stop
talking about the mystery artist,</i>


01:21:39.786 --> 01:21:42.506
<i>with many asking
who is Molly Twist</i>


01:21:42.537 --> 01:21:45.578
<i>and when and where
will all of her work appear.</i>


01:21:45.608 --> 01:21:48.969
<i>Dealers are said to be willing
to offer up to 50,000</i>


01:21:49.000 --> 01:21:52.009
<i>to anyone with
an original Twist painting.</i>


01:22:09.512 --> 01:22:11.113
Cheers, Nancy.


01:22:13.129 --> 01:22:15.977
Call me that again, Oliver,
and I will twist something you don't like.


01:22:18.249 --> 01:22:20.298
All right, quit canoodling.


01:22:22.952 --> 01:22:26.058
So, are you gonna stick
with us, kid?


01:22:26.089 --> 01:22:27.882
Come on,
you know you wanna.


01:22:27.914 --> 01:22:30.314
Look, if I'm gonna be
staying around,


01:22:30.345 --> 01:22:32.361
we gotta cut out all
the nonsense and go straight.


01:22:32.392 --> 01:22:35.561
- Whoa, wait.
- He's joking, right? That must be a joke.


01:22:35.593 --> 01:22:39.050
What exactly do you expect
us lot to do for a job, eh?


01:22:39.753 --> 01:22:41.706
You ever thought about
selling paintings?


01:22:42.666 --> 01:22:45.066
A bag full of Molly Twist art
is worth a few quid.


01:22:46.601 --> 01:22:47.594
Hmm?


01:22:48.393 --> 01:22:51.689
<i>Like I said, no singing,
no dancing.</i>


01:22:51.722 --> 01:22:53.802
<i>But maybe I was wrong about
the happy ending.</i>


01:22:54.762 --> 01:22:57.514
<i>I know these people.
I belong with them.</i>


01:25:45.482 --> 01:25:48.107
